WEBVTT

00:00.167 --> 00:02.245
- [Voiceover] Let k equal four,

00:02.245 --> 00:05.961
so that f of x is equal to one
over x squared minus four x.

00:05.961 --> 00:08.738
Determine whether f
has a relative minimum,

00:08.738 --> 00:12.449
a relative maximum, or
neither at x equals two.

00:12.449 --> 00:15.329
Justify your answer.

00:15.329 --> 00:16.051
All right.

00:16.051 --> 00:18.883
Well, if f of x is equal
to this, then f prime of x,

00:18.883 --> 00:21.655
they gave us f prime of x in terms of k.

00:21.655 --> 00:24.808
So f prime of x

00:24.808 --> 00:26.123
is going to be equal to,

00:26.123 --> 00:27.237
in this case k is four.

00:27.237 --> 00:29.756
So it's gonna be four minus two x.

00:29.756 --> 00:31.428
Four minus two x.

00:31.428 --> 00:35.138
Over x squared minus

00:35.138 --> 00:37.388
four x squared

00:37.388 --> 00:40.763
minus four x

00:40.763 --> 00:42.586
minus four x squared.

00:42.586 --> 00:45.595
So now we know f of x
and we know f prime of x.

00:45.595 --> 00:47.879
And if we were looking for relative minima

00:47.879 --> 00:49.329
or relative maxima,

00:49.329 --> 00:53.676
we would be interested in
points, and critical points.

00:53.676 --> 00:57.124
And especially where f
prime of x is equal to zero.

00:57.124 --> 01:01.591
And so if we said f prime
of x is equal to zero,

01:01.591 --> 01:04.982
well, we would say, when does
this numerator equal zero?

01:04.982 --> 01:09.326
And so you could say, when does
four minus two x equal zero?

01:09.326 --> 01:12.919
You add two x to both sides,
you get four is equal to two x.

01:12.919 --> 01:16.774
Or x is equal to two, x is equal to two.

01:16.774 --> 01:17.868
And they told us that.

01:17.868 --> 01:19.608
Or I guess we've confirmed that

01:19.608 --> 01:23.830
at f prime of two

01:23.830 --> 01:26.857
does indeed equal to zero.

01:26.857 --> 01:29.881
So this is definitely
an interesting point.

01:29.881 --> 01:32.207
So let's think about whether before,

01:32.207 --> 01:34.087
when x is less than two,

01:34.087 --> 01:37.187
is f prime of x increasing or decreasing?

01:37.187 --> 01:39.149
And then when x is greater than two,

01:39.149 --> 01:41.727
is f prime of x increasing or decreasing?

01:41.727 --> 01:44.792
And that will let us know if
this is a minima or a maxima.

01:44.792 --> 01:45.940
So let's say,

01:45.940 --> 01:50.715
so when x is less than two,

01:50.715 --> 01:52.508
we could test something out.

01:52.508 --> 01:54.704
We could say f prime of,

01:54.704 --> 01:57.770
so let's just say f prime of one.

01:57.770 --> 02:00.323
So if x is less than two.

02:00.323 --> 02:01.208
You know, you actually don't even

02:01.208 --> 02:02.822
have to test f prime of one.

02:02.822 --> 02:03.927
Ii mean, you could if you want.

02:03.927 --> 02:06.659
You would have four minus two.

02:06.659 --> 02:08.211
Four minus two times one.

02:08.211 --> 02:10.539
So that's going to be positive.

02:10.539 --> 02:11.704
And then this down over here

02:11.704 --> 02:14.095
is always going to be non-negative.

02:14.095 --> 02:16.527
Because you have a
squared right over here.

02:16.527 --> 02:18.330
So when x is less than two,

02:18.330 --> 02:22.369
f prime of x is greater than zero.

02:22.369 --> 02:25.494
And you could try this out with
different exes if you like.

02:25.494 --> 02:27.378
You could say, for example,

02:27.378 --> 02:29.799
for example,

02:30.843 --> 02:33.682
f prime of one is equal to

02:33.682 --> 02:36.017
four minus two, which is two

02:36.017 --> 02:39.704
over one minus four.

02:39.704 --> 02:41.931
Which is negative three, but then squared.

02:41.931 --> 02:44.965
Is equal to two ninths.

02:44.965 --> 02:46.387
And then we could say

02:47.227 --> 02:52.227
when x is greater than two,

02:52.760 --> 02:54.397
f prime of x,

02:55.407 --> 02:57.160
f prime of x.

02:57.160 --> 02:58.903
Well, when x is greater than two,

02:58.903 --> 03:02.026
you're gonna have four minus two times

03:02.026 --> 03:04.337
something larger than four.

03:04.337 --> 03:05.812
So this is going to be negative.

03:05.812 --> 03:08.097
So f prime of x is going
to be less than zero.

03:08.097 --> 03:09.855
Up here's gonna be negative.

03:09.855 --> 03:11.646
Down here's not going to be negative.

03:11.646 --> 03:14.606
And so f prime of x is
going to be less than zero.

03:14.606 --> 03:18.711
So if we are increasing
as we approach something,

03:18.711 --> 03:20.901
and then our slope is zero.

03:20.901 --> 03:22.929
And then we are decreasing,

03:22.929 --> 03:25.937
well then this is going
to be a maximum point.

03:25.937 --> 03:28.508
So that means that

03:28.508 --> 03:30.281
we have a maximum,

03:31.121 --> 03:32.703
maximum point

03:33.663 --> 03:34.585
point

03:34.585 --> 03:37.112
at x is equal

03:37.112 --> 03:40.002
at x is equal to,

03:40.002 --> 03:41.767
or we could say, yes.

03:41.767 --> 03:44.824
That we have, f has a relative maximum,

03:44.824 --> 03:47.220
relative maximum

03:47.220 --> 03:49.578
at x equals,

03:49.578 --> 03:51.042
at x equals two.

03:51.042 --> 03:52.409
Actually, let's make it right.

03:52.409 --> 03:55.611
X has a relative maximum.

03:55.611 --> 03:56.962
We're just going to use
the words they are using.

03:56.962 --> 03:58.627
Relative,

03:58.627 --> 04:01.705
relative maximum

04:01.705 --> 04:05.019
at x is equal to two.

04:05.019 --> 04:06.956
Now another way that you
could have tried to do it

04:06.956 --> 04:07.901
