upwards or downwards.

04:14.043 --> 04:15.928
But taking the second derivative of this,

04:15.928 --> 04:17.141
it gets quite hairy.

04:17.141 --> 04:18.849
And any time you're taking the AP test

04:18.849 --> 04:20.016
and you find yourself going down

04:20.016 --> 04:21.599
a really, really hairy path.

04:21.599 --> 04:23.583
Like taking the derivative of,

04:23.583 --> 04:25.650
or like taking the second derivative of f,

04:25.650 --> 04:27.860
which would be the first
derivative of f prime.

04:27.860 --> 04:30.598
Any time you see yourself going
down a hairy path like that,

04:30.598 --> 04:34.468
it might work, but it's
probably not the optimal path.

04:34.468 --> 04:36.186
So an easier way is to just think,

04:36.186 --> 04:39.345
okay, well what is f prime
doing as we approach this?

04:39.345 --> 04:40.264
Or another way is thinking,

04:40.264 --> 04:43.650
